NOTE: how to setup the Lumiera-Website

The Website is built with Asciidoc (the old python flavour).
Thus you need to install `apt install asciidoc`

There is a script `build-website.sh` to generate the HTML-pages
from the Asciidoc sources. Furthermore there is a python script
to build the navigation-menue (and this script is invoked
automatically from build-website.sh)

Typically you want to integrate this build-script as a Git-hook,
so that the Website is automatically rebuilt on each Git push.


However -- we integrate some subdirectories from other Git repositories,
which also provide Asciidoc sources. Most notably, the main Lumiera repository
holds the complete technical documentation.

Thus you need to provide extra working directories for these additional
components, and check our an appropriate branch there. And in addition to that,
you need to set up a symlink *manually* to point to those extra components.

(In the future we plan to use git-submodules eventually)


git://git.lumiera.org/lumiera_documentation

ln -s <checkout-of-this-repo>/doc documentation



Furthermore, a Debian Apt-Depot for DEB packages is included.
The setup of this repository is managed by the "reprepro" tool,
which is part of the Debian distribution (apt install reprepro).

The configuration for this repository is maintained in this Git-Repo
git://git.lumiera.org/debian/lumiera

you need to checkout branch "depot" and then build the repository
with the reprepro tool. However, some index and information page
in Asciidoc format is directly included on that branch, in the
file 'depot/index.txt'

Typically you'll maintain this DEB repo locally and publish the
contents of the 'depot' directory with `rsync`

For this to work, you need to setup a symlink

ln -s <depot-directory> debian


